  "requiredFootnotes": {
    "F01": "One sealed ghostty-webgpu 0.3.21 runtime at fb67ac08ded224fd6579389a23796e015ee23d5c. Publish the cell-specific browser, terminal count, ticks, harness generation, cadence, condition and geometry. This is a scoped observation, not a cross-machine normalized result.",
    "F02": "Each numerical cell has two chronological actor-paired Ghostty/counterpart ratios; lower is less recorded work. The median is the median of those two ratios, not a ratio of summed counters. Projected order is ABBA or BAAB. Shared nested actor windows correlate cells and can make paired windows nonadjacent. No significance, universal winner or candidate KEEP decision follows.",
    "F03": "The benchmark observer is enabled and its overhead is uncalibrated; no overhead is subtracted. Native reader capability calibration is separate and was checked. R08 prepares fixture inputs before the measurement window.",
    "F04": "allChrome covers the endpoint-recorded Chrome process family, including CPU activity in Chrome’s GPU process. It excludes GPU-device, display, whole-machine and unrelated-process energy. Sequential native snapshots enclose CDP CPU snapshots and are non-atomic. Endpoint PID/type/start checks cannot detect a process born and gone wholly between endpoints.",
    "F05": "Qualification checks equal public writes and UTF-8 bytes, the registered final retained output or common tail, Unicode cell widths where registered, logical settlement, stable same-actor PNGs and actual drawing/DOM geometry. This does not prove identical raster, typography, intermediate operations, GPU completion or physical presentation. A logical two-RAF endpoint is not a GPU/display fence.",
    "F07": "xterm 6 Unicode-emoji cells use @xterm/addon-unicode11 0.9.0 and active Unicode version 11 before output. Exact owner text and cell-width/boundary digests are checked. Canvas xterm 5.5 uses its separately identified Unicode11 addon 0.8.0.",
    "F09": "Mac scored metrics are kernel-estimated process CPU energy and retired instructions, all Chrome. Total cycles, CPU seconds, P/E placement, effective clocks and cluster CPI/IPC are diagnostics. Per-pair instruction, placement and within-cluster CPI factors are supplied. Cycle/speed headlines require a matched-placement protocol. A within-cluster CPI rise is disclosed without an unmeasured GC, compilation, stall or thread-role attribution.",
    "F13": "Publish the actual drawing-buffer size and DPR. Standing uses DPR2 on Mac/Pi and DPR1 on Linux. In particular Linux standing WebGPU uses 280×228 pixels, whereas the earlier r12-webgpu controls use 560×456 pixels at DPR2: four times the pixel count. The two sessions are not the same raster experiment.",
    "F14": "This review does not verify automatic renderer selection, an inherent platform limitation, faster physical presentation, uninstrumented behavior or a universal/all-workloads win. Rule 37 exceptions require separate attribution and automatic-selection evidence.",
    "F15": "An unavailable/unqualified cell has no publishable qualified numerical ratio. Keep it visibly unavailable with its receipt-backed reason; it is neither a measured loss nor a win, and must not be dropped from inventory or borrowed from another build/condition.",
    "F16": "Custody is assessed from saved per-run and final receipts: bounded Mac controllers and owned-prefix cleanup, private Linux compositor/no-card-node/no-DRM-master cleanup, and stopped Pi browser/service with restored ondemand governor. This is not a new live-host custody check.",
    "F17": "The Mac DOM Unicode r02 was registered prospectively with unchanged conditions, but it repeated DOM windows whose r01 per-window and same-actor PNG gates passed. Only xterm DOM failed the repeated-PNG gate. Strict per-window no-valid-replay compliance fails for this excluded cell; neither attempt contributes to the 85 qualified numerical cells."
  },
